                "senses": [
                    {
                        "sense_id": "67508585-b4c2-31e5-9f45-56b2f1fcd9bd",
                        "entry_id": "5d201321-ce39-3587-80c9-3c379144d523",
                        "glosses": [
                            "неол. город, основная часть работоспособного населения которого трудится на одном или нескольких (немногих) градообразующих предприятиях, как правило, одного профиля"
                        ],
                        "tags": [],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "71457ce9-6421-4bf9-bbd2-71739b7dd85c",
                                "sense_id": "67508585-b4c2-31e5-9f45-56b2f1fcd9bd",
                                "text": "По подсчётам Института региональной политики, 460 городов в России (около 40 % от общего числа городов) являются моногородами."
                            }
                        ]
                    }
                ],
                "translations": [
                    {
                        "translation_id": "98a72050-6339-48da-976d-7c29c7564a1d",
                        "source_entry_id": "5d201321-ce39-3587-80c9-3c379144d523",
                        "source_sense_id": "67508585-b4c2-31e5-9f45-56b2f1fcd9bd",
                        "target_lang_word": "mono-city",
                        "target_lang_code": "en",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": []
                    },
                    {
                        "translation_id": "ae0d8d1b-fbf2-4f93-a039-e3fd46a49afc",
                        "source_entry_id": "5d201321-ce39-3587-80c9-3c379144d523",
                        "source_sense_id": "67508585-b4c2-31e5-9f45-56b2f1fcd9bd",
                        "target_lang_word": "monotown",
                        "target_lang_code": "en",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "monotown",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "9da9ff6d-983e-36e5-a0cc-7a443cf96749",
                                        "entry_id": "7331a21d-fcde-307a-8eca-c709595d2a40",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "A town or city whose economy is dominated by a single industry or company."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": []
                                    }
                                ]
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "translation_id": "ac360cfe-5f15-4d9d-b2aa-a32ddf89670e",
                        "source_entry_id": "5d201321-ce39-3587-80c9-3c379144d523",
                        "source_sense_id": "67508585-b4c2-31e5-9f45-56b2f1fcd9bd",
                        "target_lang_word": "company town",
                        "target_lang_code": "en",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "company town",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "a490e3e0-471a-3fd5-b06b-dc1a5a84ffdc",
                                        "entry_id": "3d0ec4e8-424f-3d5d-b6e4-edab395ac78a",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "A town, city, or other municipality in which a single large business has a controlling influence over the economy and, sometimes, over the societal structure and the local government."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "idiomatic"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "b040179b-40e8-4211-9fbd-372762625a7b",
                                                "sense_id": "a490e3e0-471a-3fd5-b06b-dc1a5a84ffdc",
                                                "text": "The workmen lived farther along the line, in a sort of company town, which at present greatly resembled a Western mining-camp, though ultimately it was to be a bungalow town."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "e67e9fc0-78eb-4f7a-9de6-ced097f475a1",
                                                "sense_id": "a490e3e0-471a-3fd5-b06b-dc1a5a84ffdc",
                                                "text": "Now here we have a company town depicted by our authority in the UMW [United Mine Workers] as one of the worst imaginable company towns, where the employer ran the schools, the local administration of justice, and even the churches."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "1ee8bebb-f5e6-444d-b447-0d3f96b5e5e3",
                                                "sense_id": "a490e3e0-471a-3fd5-b06b-dc1a5a84ffdc",
                                                "text": "Back in the days when Poughkeepsie was a company town and the company was International Business Machines, it wasn't unusual for 18-year-olds in Poughkeepsie to go straight from high school to I.B.M."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "0c28101a-a037-49da-9122-c027d394c790",
                                                "sense_id": "a490e3e0-471a-3fd5-b06b-dc1a5a84ffdc",
                                                "text": "The firm's sprawling factory complexes lie only a short distance from the town center, and, as in any company town, the paychecks of Toyota employees are the main source of support for its restaurants and shops."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "translation_id": "3bd44e36-4e45-4ff1-82a1-0de3788d140d",
                        "source_entry_id": "5d201321-ce39-3587-80c9-3c379144d523",
                        "source_sense_id": "67508585-b4c2-31e5-9f45-56b2f1fcd9bd",
                        "target_lang_word": "monoville",
                        "target_lang_code": "fr",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "monoville",
                                "target_lang_code": "fr",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "b88bf215-8501-3f58-8a30-0bd63e7616e2",
                                        "entry_id": "a3c4d5f0-0af9-3a62-a69b-ee89400206db",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Cité industrielle de monoactivité, ville mono-industrielle."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "b40f6fdd-d626-4618-85e5-82cac549556e",
                                                "sense_id": "b88bf215-8501-3f58-8a30-0bd63e7616e2",
                                                "text": "Sorte de cité modèle dans les années 1970, Toyota City est devenue une « monoville », entièrement organisée autour des seules activités de la société Toyota mais aussi complètement dépendante de ses résultats et de son développement."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "732ff98d-0621-45b9-be62-26d604593cf9",
                                                "sense_id": "b88bf215-8501-3f58-8a30-0bd63e7616e2",
                                                "text": "Les premières victimes de la crise en Russie sont les \"monovilles\", mammouths industriels hérités de l'époque soviétique et organisés autour d'une seule activité. On en dénombre seize dans la région de Kirov, où les plus gros employeurs demeurent les usines obsolètes du complexe militaro-industriel."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "d0e98fa5-7835-4f3a-ba89-5f429e69d800",
                                                "sense_id": "b88bf215-8501-3f58-8a30-0bd63e7616e2",
                                                "text": "Selon lui, le gouvernement, \"doté d'une administration qui tourne à vide\", est incapable de sauver ne serait-ce qu'une partie des \"monovilles\"."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            }
                        ]
                    }
                ],
